WEBVTT

00:13.650 --> 00:15.840
This... is really bad.

00:16.330 --> 00:19.170
Three healers won't be enough to handle it.

00:21.260 --> 00:23.020
<i>Those wounds are awful.</i>

00:23.020 --> 00:26.750
<i>Fights with adventurers can get this bad?</i>

00:27.380 --> 00:30.900
Those injuries... They were attacked 
by a carnivorous beast.

00:31.420 --> 00:34.090
And the cuts to their torsos
were caused by wind magic.

00:34.380 --> 00:36.740
Beasts and magic?

00:37.320 --> 00:38.750
I'll lend a hand!

00:39.150 --> 00:40.710
Please continue praying!

00:41.490 --> 00:44.170
<i>I don't have any magic, but I'll pray too!</i>

00:44.690 --> 00:48.310
Recumora Dieusahé Cresiolle.

00:49.160 --> 00:51.620
<i>Healing magic calls upon the Goddess's power.</i>

00:51.620 --> 00:53.510
<i>Our prayers will strengthen it.</i>

00:54.320 --> 00:56.870
<i>Please, may they be saved!</i>

01:08.160 --> 01:09.750
The pain's gone...?

01:10.410 --> 01:11.860
Thank goodness.

01:11.860 --> 01:13.610
How incredible!

01:14.300 --> 01:16.320
If you're injured, gather around!

01:16.320 --> 01:17.800
I'll heal you all at once!

01:18.100 --> 01:20.510
Did you apprehend who caused all this?

01:20.830 --> 01:22.650
They're in the dungeons below.

01:22.650 --> 01:28.220
One of the culprits is a beastmaster,
and we also had to isolate his beast.

01:29.440 --> 01:33.420
<i>Another job that specializes in beasts, 
like what Lestin and the Beast Knights do.</i>

01:33.420 --> 01:35.440
<i>Except they don't just ride them...</i>

01:35.440 --> 01:39.110
<i>They take advantage of animals' 
abilities to kill and track.</i>

01:39.110 --> 01:41.750
<i>They use their beasts as partners
 on their adventures.</i>

01:42.520 --> 01:47.900
I see... So we have hold-out criminals 
calling themselves adventurers.

01:59.840 --> 02:04.720
<b><i>Fluffy Paradise</i></b>

03:21.630 --> 03:26.640
<b><i>Episode 11   The Path I Chose</i></b>

03:24.810 --> 03:27.020
I'm so exhausted...

03:27.250 --> 03:31.870
<i>We had all that trouble involving the 
beastmaster right after visiting the kobolds.</i>

03:31.870 --> 03:34.530
<i>That's a lot for a little kid!</i>

03:35.400 --> 03:37.800
Good night, Ralf...

03:38.460 --> 03:39.710
Healran!

03:43.620 --> 03:46.030
A-Are you okay?

03:46.360 --> 03:48.750
I would never blow my cover.

03:49.040 --> 03:51.820
Then could you tell us why 
you were with the knights

03:51.820 --> 03:54.310
and report any information you've gathered?

03:54.310 --> 03:55.160
Yes.

03:55.910 --> 03:59.060
While investigating the collusion
between the adventurers and knights,

03:59.060 --> 04:01.530
I wound up being questioned by the knights.

04:01.530 --> 04:04.070
I got out of it by telling them
 I had a falling out

04:04.070 --> 04:06.890
with my adventurer buddies 
and was looking for work.

04:07.190 --> 04:10.460
They then recommended me for a desk job,

04:10.460 --> 04:13.680
and now, I'm investigating the 
knighthood from the inside.

04:13.680 --> 04:17.610
<i>I can't believe it! The knights
he talked to were way too nice!</i>

04:17.610 --> 04:21.320
I have indeed found the
 regional commander to be shady.

04:21.650 --> 04:26.570
He's been stealing relief aid, embezzling 
funds, and taking bribes from adventurers...

04:26.570 --> 04:28.400
All clearly dubious acts.

04:28.400 --> 04:30.570
Why are adventurers involved, though?

04:30.570 --> 04:32.740
To make them look good at the guild.

04:32.740 --> 04:37.050
If they pay him, 
he'll overreport their achievements.

04:37.320 --> 04:38.870
Do you have any proof of this?

04:39.280 --> 04:41.500
I haven't been able to track
 the flow of money.

04:42.450 --> 04:44.980
We need some physical evidence.

04:44.980 --> 04:47.830
I'll try to follow the money trail, but...

04:47.830 --> 04:49.670
That could be difficult.

04:51.990 --> 04:54.820
The knights are known 
for their shoddy management.

04:54.820 --> 04:57.280
Even back home, I hear
commanders are always arguing

04:57.280 --> 05:00.080
with the accounting department
about how funds are used.

05:00.080 --> 05:01.820
So the regional knights must also be...

05:03.780 --> 05:04.870
That's it!

05:04.870 --> 05:06.720
They're submitting inflated claims!

05:06.720 --> 05:12.320
Yes. The knights regularly overorder
 supplies in case of emergencies.

05:12.590 --> 05:17.030
If we go through their orders and deliveries,
we might find something!

05:17.870 --> 05:18.880
Healran.

05:20.340 --> 05:23.470
I leave you with my royal crest.

05:26.670 --> 05:28.180
Don't let them get away.

05:28.630 --> 05:29.420
I won't.

05:30.290 --> 05:34.380
<i>Now that he's under the auspices of both
the Osphe family </i>and<i> the royal family,</i>

05:34.380 --> 05:37.270
<i>Healran's life will be in even more jeopardy.</i>

05:39.250 --> 05:44.440
Healran, as long as you can find proof, Will
 and the others will take care of the rest.

05:44.440 --> 05:48.250
So make sure you put your safety first.

05:48.250 --> 05:49.690
I understand.

05:50.260 --> 05:52.970
<i>Please protect him, spirits.</i>

05:53.700 --> 05:56.640
Okay, now that that's settled, 
let's get you to bed.

05:57.130 --> 05:59.590
You're getting into the
habit of staying up too late.

06:00.590 --> 06:02.850
I will also take my leave.

06:02.850 --> 06:03.770
Healran.

06:04.170 --> 06:04.870
Yes?

06:05.240 --> 06:08.590
Make sure you don't do anything 
that'll make Neema sad.

06:08.590 --> 06:14.560
I owe Lady Neema for taking me in. 
I will do everything in my power for her.

06:15.710 --> 06:17.810
You're my friend, Healran!

06:20.440 --> 06:22.230
Thank you very much.

06:26.490 --> 06:30.130
<i>I never knew that Healran 
could smile like that.</i>

06:33.630 --> 06:37.070
Red Hlaada will be arriving tomorrow.

06:37.600 --> 06:39.630
Things will be set in motion the day after.

06:39.980 --> 06:43.700
This is probably going to be hard on Neema.

06:44.120 --> 06:47.180
It's unavoidable. 
This is the path that she chose...

06:48.650 --> 06:51.610
even if she doesn't realize it.

06:58.200 --> 07:00.010
Quiet, everyone!

07:00.770 --> 07:04.340
This is our last strategy meeting for
tomorrow and it's really important!

07:07.200 --> 07:09.540
Are the children in the way?

07:09.540 --> 07:11.010
They're fine.

07:11.010 --> 07:14.900
Everyone needs to know what's going 
on, even if they aren't fighting.

07:16.880 --> 07:19.510
Foremost, I need all of you to understand

07:19.510 --> 07:24.040
that this battle is so we can move
 your pack somewhere safe.

07:24.740 --> 07:27.730
Also, do not forget that we are here

07:27.730 --> 07:32.310
to help you because that is Nefertima's wish.

07:33.830 --> 07:35.050
Let's get right into it.

07:35.050 --> 07:39.360
The extermination squad includes
 53 knights and two healers.

07:39.360 --> 07:42.030
The adventurers have 34 melee fighters,

07:42.510 --> 07:48.730
28 mages, ten mid-range fighters, 
eight healers, and twelve scouts,

07:48.730 --> 07:50.510
totaling 92 members in fifteen parties.

07:50.950 --> 07:54.140
Note that this does not include Red Hlaada,

07:54.140 --> 07:58.110
as we have no detailed intel on them,
 or the knights on our side.

07:55.410 --> 07:57.740
<i>Will is the prince of this kingdom.</i>

07:58.110 --> 08:02.770
<i>He can't sacrifice his knights or people
 for the sake of monsters.</i>

07:58.470 --> 08:02.890
With safety in mind, we must dispatch
 the adventurers thusly...

08:02.770 --> 08:05.990
<i>We've thought this through 
as thoroughly as possible.</i>

08:05.990 --> 08:07.770
When we hit the designated casualties,

08:07.770 --> 08:10.770
Ralfreed, who is in the extermination 
squad, will order a retreat.

08:11.520 --> 08:13.630
<i>Am I okay with this?</i>

08:13.630 --> 08:17.700
<i>Can we really protect the kobolds this way?</i>

08:17.700 --> 08:18.460
Neema.

08:19.670 --> 08:22.140
Is there anything you'd like to say as well?

08:25.440 --> 08:26.640
Shinki.

08:29.510 --> 08:33.600
There will most likely
 be fatalities in this battle.

08:34.990 --> 08:38.620
Everyone participating needs to be prepared!

08:49.480 --> 08:51.180
Stop making that face.

08:51.180 --> 08:53.950
Everyone will panic if they 
see their leader looking uneasy.

08:53.950 --> 08:58.180
Don't let them know you're troubled, 
though you should remain circumspect.

08:58.490 --> 09:00.890
But once you've chosen your path,
 do not waver.

09:02.630 --> 09:05.110
Is that what you always do, Will?

09:05.620 --> 09:07.050
Of course.

09:07.050 --> 09:10.290
I'm going to follow in my father's 
footsteps and become king someday.

09:11.240 --> 09:13.880
I constantly question myself.

09:13.880 --> 09:20.050
Will my choices betray the hopes 
of the people around me and my citizens?

09:21.130 --> 09:25.100
But what I decide firmly, 
I have no problem giving voice to.

09:25.640 --> 09:28.280
You need to think more before you speak.

09:28.820 --> 09:32.810
<i>He's right. I need to prepare myself, too.</i>

09:32.810 --> 09:34.260
<i>But how...?</i>

09:35.460 --> 09:37.210
A report from Ralf?

09:39.010 --> 09:40.260
What's wrong?

09:40.260 --> 09:44.190
This isn't good. The beastmaster and the person 
he was fighting have been released.

09:44.470 --> 09:45.510
Why?

09:45.510 --> 09:47.520
To bolster their forces.

09:48.090 --> 09:53.650
Curse that fox of a commander. 
How dare he overstep his authority?

09:54.070 --> 09:57.670
<i>It seems like the situation 
just keeps getting worse.</i>

09:58.650 --> 10:01.050
<i>The plan begins tomorrow...</i>

10:01.880 --> 10:05.890
<i>God, what am I supposed to do?</i>

10:12.430 --> 10:14.300
Okay, Neema, be careful.

10:14.760 --> 10:15.590
I will.

10:17.190 --> 10:19.990
<i>After everything, I couldn't sleep well.</i>

10:21.580 --> 10:25.140
Hey, that tickles! What's the matter?

10:25.140 --> 10:27.730
They're trying to cheer you up.

10:27.730 --> 10:29.650
Mr. Fighter Leader...

10:30.050 --> 10:35.280
I cannot blame you for worrying. 
But we're with you.

10:35.860 --> 10:37.850
You're not scared?

10:39.340 --> 10:43.310
I've lived a very long time in a world
 where death may find me at any moment.

10:43.310 --> 10:46.480
I tore my fear down to size many moons ago.

10:46.480 --> 10:50.470
And if I ever let it get the best of me,

10:50.470 --> 10:53.460
I wouldn't be able to protect these two.

10:53.830 --> 10:58.670
Of course, I plan to protect your life 
as well. Even if it means my own.

10:59.490 --> 11:03.070
We've chosen to put our fate in your hands.

11:03.070 --> 11:06.130
We made that decision ourselves.

11:06.130 --> 11:10.890
You've just gotta do what you've gotta do.

11:16.990 --> 11:18.100
Right!

11:19.520 --> 11:22.620
The battle is nigh, 
but I'm changing our target priorities.

11:22.620 --> 11:27.210
We've learned that Red Hlaada has arrived
and the beastmaster has been released.

11:28.010 --> 11:32.230
The beastmaster gravely injured many knights
and should be considered dangerous.

11:33.020 --> 11:36.880
Make sure to incapacitate him first 
and hand him over to the inquisitor.

11:37.920 --> 11:39.090
Lady Neema.

11:40.790 --> 11:42.010
Are you okay?

11:45.210 --> 11:47.600
Thank you. I'm fine.

11:47.600 --> 11:49.280
<i>I need to get a grip.</i>

11:49.280 --> 11:51.610
<i>I'm the one who sowed these seeds, after all.</i>

11:53.350 --> 11:54.760
What's the matter?

11:55.200 --> 11:55.890
They're here.

12:03.540 --> 12:05.030
The extermination squad!

12:13.520 --> 12:16.120
Our enemy is the kobolds 
with a werewolf among them!

12:16.120 --> 12:17.830
Don't let your guard down!

12:21.750 --> 12:23.160
Say, Yuga...

12:23.160 --> 12:24.470
What is it, Luck?

12:24.470 --> 12:27.820
I think there's something more to this job.

12:27.820 --> 12:33.010
I agree. The closer we got to Lenice, 
the more hardship we encountered.

12:33.010 --> 12:34.430
Probably just a coincidence.

12:34.430 --> 12:36.980
Well, I can't say for certain it wasn't...

12:37.720 --> 12:39.140
<i>Still, she has a point.</i>

12:39.140 --> 12:43.940
<i>Our rations spoiled in that sudden downpour, 
we got lost once we entered the forest...</i>

12:43.940 --> 12:44.700
<i>It's like...</i>

12:45.060 --> 12:48.510
It's like some invisible force
 is getting in our way.

12:48.510 --> 12:51.660
Well, my nose knows for sure.

12:52.090 --> 12:57.360
There are folks around here who
reek of malice and money.

13:03.960 --> 13:08.000
<i>The squad is about to reach the checkpoint
for putting the plan into effect.</i>

13:08.300 --> 13:11.400
Shinki, Lars, are you ready?

13:14.780 --> 13:16.920
I'm also counting on you, Herbs.

13:19.190 --> 13:22.880
<i>This will all ride on how many troops 
we can incapacitate out of the gate!</i>

13:23.610 --> 13:24.500
Let's go.

13:24.500 --> 13:25.220
Yeah.

13:26.350 --> 13:28.730
Three. Two.

13:27.310 --> 13:31.190
<i>We'll have Shinki conjure a dense fog
 with the spirits to obscure their vision.</i>

13:29.540 --> 13:30.550
One...

13:29.870 --> 13:31.200
Wh-What the?

13:31.200 --> 13:32.160
Zero!

13:34.330 --> 13:37.790
<i>Lars will amplify Will's air raid.</i>

13:39.400 --> 13:40.250
Get down!

13:48.260 --> 13:49.870
Kobolds?!

13:49.870 --> 13:52.080
We're toast if the high-ranking ones are here.

13:52.080 --> 13:54.270
If you see the werewolf, take it out first!

13:56.420 --> 13:58.010
Damn it! I can't hear anything!

13:58.010 --> 14:00.780
It's no use! We can't repel 
this fog with magic!

14:00.210 --> 14:04.680
<i>While the spirits are helping us, 
we'll take advantage of the confusion.</i>

14:00.780 --> 14:02.430
Do something!

14:02.430 --> 14:04.680
Stay close together until 
we get out of the fog!

14:05.360 --> 14:09.610
<i>The Herbs will incapacitate 
as many people as possible.</i>

14:10.050 --> 14:11.800
Bring the adventurers over here!

14:14.030 --> 14:16.760
<i>The undercover knights are making their move!</i>

14:19.100 --> 14:21.430
Apparently the beastmaster 
has been captured.

14:26.690 --> 14:28.050
Where's the beast?

14:31.270 --> 14:31.930
Sic 'em!

14:33.560 --> 14:34.710
Look out!

14:39.190 --> 14:40.640
Gratia?

14:46.250 --> 14:48.230
I-Is he dead?

14:48.230 --> 14:50.190
No, he's just paralyzed.

14:50.800 --> 14:52.360
That was amazing, Gratia!

14:52.760 --> 14:55.340
<i>I guess she's venomous!</i>

14:55.340 --> 14:57.470
I think I heard voices over here!

14:57.470 --> 14:58.390
Is it kobolds?

14:58.390 --> 14:59.960
Don't let them get away this time!

14:58.560 --> 15:00.390
They're onto us now.

15:00.390 --> 15:01.530
Begin the next phase!

15:09.690 --> 15:11.200
Wh-What the?!

15:11.200 --> 15:12.760
Did the kobolds set this trap?

15:16.400 --> 15:17.430
Wh-What now?!

15:17.430 --> 15:18.640
There are blades mixed in!

15:18.640 --> 15:22.290
Onward! We're breaking through this fog!

15:30.120 --> 15:32.120
A-A slime?

15:30.120 --> 15:32.120
I-It's melting my stuff!

15:30.620 --> 15:31.780
Save me!

15:32.330 --> 15:35.050
<i>Haku's down at the bottom!</i>

15:35.050 --> 15:38.210
You can eat all of the enemies' 
weapons and equipment, okay?

15:38.830 --> 15:40.910
See? I told you.

15:40.910 --> 15:44.300
It's too dangerous to move
recklessly at times like this.

15:44.540 --> 15:46.120
Seira, save them.

15:54.020 --> 15:55.820
She's casting Central Pillar!

15:56.830 --> 16:00.280
<i>The only thing we can use 
against an intermediate earth spell</i>

16:00.280 --> 16:02.570
<i>would be an unaligned spell
or an advanced fire spell,</i>

16:02.570 --> 16:04.610
<i>which is earth's opposing element.</i>

16:04.610 --> 16:05.560
<i>In that case...</i>

16:05.560 --> 16:07.520
Sol! Please help us!

16:09.320 --> 16:10.330
I cannot.

16:10.780 --> 16:14.270
If I do from this location,
some of you would be harmed as well.

16:14.270 --> 16:15.750
<i>Oh no!</i>

16:15.750 --> 16:18.210
Their vanguard approaches! Engage them!

16:19.890 --> 16:23.270
The kobolds are upon us! Look alive!

16:29.190 --> 16:30.680
<i>A bear beastperson?!</i>

16:30.680 --> 16:32.880
That's Red Hlaada.

16:33.260 --> 16:34.350
That's them?

16:38.210 --> 16:40.350
Did you notice, Yuga?

16:40.350 --> 16:44.720
The kobolds... No, this whole 
battle reeks of humans.

16:45.560 --> 16:50.310
I don't know who it is, 
but someone's helping them out.

16:52.310 --> 16:53.540
Look out!

16:54.220 --> 16:55.470
<i>A child?</i>

16:56.630 --> 16:59.580
<i>So I wasn't imagining things.</i>

16:59.960 --> 17:01.040
What should we do?

17:04.060 --> 17:06.020
<i>A third of our forces are injured.</i>

17:06.020 --> 17:08.160
<i>Most will be back on their feet soon.</i>

17:08.160 --> 17:11.060
<i>The problem is those who've lost their gear.</i>

17:14.410 --> 17:17.740
Everyone with intermediate magic,
protect the wounded and the healers!

17:19.280 --> 17:20.970
Anyone with advanced magic, advance!

17:21.260 --> 17:22.340
Commander Noctis!

17:22.340 --> 17:24.450
Please lend us five knights as guards.

17:25.030 --> 17:27.280
Let's go, vanguard adventurers!

17:28.230 --> 17:29.230
They're so strong...

17:31.050 --> 17:32.920
Don't look away, Neema.

17:33.390 --> 17:35.280
This is the path you chose.

17:36.670 --> 17:40.900
Even if everyone else forgets, 
you must always remember this.

17:52.630 --> 17:55.130
They have mages with advanced fire magic?

17:55.650 --> 17:57.810
Luck, we're falling back for now.

18:00.020 --> 18:02.420
Our enemies are tougher than we thought.

18:02.730 --> 18:05.880
We should retreat and prioritize defense
 while tending to the wounded.

18:05.880 --> 18:09.090
We've only exterminated about half of them.

18:09.660 --> 18:12.060
This'll be pointless
if we lose our people too!

18:12.640 --> 18:15.400
<i>Actually... Despite how hard 
they've been attacking,</i>

18:15.400 --> 18:17.340
<i>we've yet to suffer any casualties?</i>

18:17.340 --> 18:19.130
<i>How is that possible?</i>

18:19.530 --> 18:23.140
<i>I'm also concerned 
that I only see knights here.</i>

18:23.140 --> 18:24.990
<i>What happened to the other adventurers?</i>

18:25.310 --> 18:30.950
You know, this whole extermination 
mission might be some kind of scheme.

18:30.950 --> 18:34.030
Pardon me. I couldn't help overhearing.

18:34.030 --> 18:35.410
Lord Ralfreed!

18:35.710 --> 18:37.830
Considering our current stalemate,

18:37.830 --> 18:40.390
I believe we could pull out 
without casualties.

18:40.390 --> 18:41.960
Right?

18:41.960 --> 18:46.350
Even if we tend to the wounded,
we'll only last as long as the healers' magic.

18:46.350 --> 18:51.530
Not to mention it's really fishy 
that there are so few wounded on our side.

18:52.420 --> 18:55.000
Do you think the kobolds 
are plotting something?

18:55.310 --> 19:00.740
Werewolves are their third evolutionary form,
 and each one has unique abilities.

19:01.170 --> 19:05.460
If theirs specializes in magic,
it may be difficult to exterminate.

19:05.770 --> 19:08.910
Evolution makes that much of a difference?

19:08.910 --> 19:12.960
Monsters are divided into those 
who can evolve and those who can't,

19:12.960 --> 19:15.230
and the number of times they evolve varies.

19:15.230 --> 19:18.430
When they reach higher evolutions,
they gain unique traits...

19:18.910 --> 19:21.300
But those are all highly individualized.

19:21.300 --> 19:24.290
They might concern strength, magic, or speed.

19:24.290 --> 19:29.890
That's exactly why I want us to get rid 
of the werewolf here and now!

19:31.490 --> 19:32.970
I suppose we've no choice.

19:33.340 --> 19:34.470
Cast a barrier, please.

19:34.470 --> 19:35.930
O-Okay.

19:41.570 --> 19:44.150
Commander Noctis 
and the members of Red Hlaada...

19:44.150 --> 19:47.660
Swear upon your names that you will 
not repeat what I'm about to tell you.

19:54.100 --> 19:55.550
Very well.

19:55.550 --> 20:00.140
I, Dylan Noctis, swear upon my name 
that I will not repeat a word of it.

20:00.490 --> 20:02.580
I, Yuga Alsto, represent Red Hlaada.

20:03.220 --> 20:05.830
We also swear not to repeat 
what we hear here.

20:06.140 --> 20:07.140
Thank you.

20:07.750 --> 20:11.820
We've discovered there's a high chance
that the increase in monster attacks

20:11.820 --> 20:16.310
in the north is being artificially
orchestrated by some organization.

20:17.270 --> 20:20.520
We haven't figured out why or who's behind it,

20:20.940 --> 20:24.740
but we've decided to call this 
mysterious organization "Runohark."

20:25.070 --> 20:28.520
So you're saying that the kobolds were 
driven here by this organization?

20:28.520 --> 20:32.040
In smaller packs, 
kobolds rarely attack humans.

20:32.040 --> 20:35.460
We can probably retreat if we can 
thin their numbers a little.

20:35.760 --> 20:39.270
But the kobolds have a human
 on their side, don't they?

20:39.270 --> 20:40.550
What do you mean?

20:40.550 --> 20:44.420
Luck mentioned that he smelled 
a human among the kobolds.

20:44.770 --> 20:46.630
Also, I thought I heard...

20:47.220 --> 20:49.110
the voice of a little girl.

20:50.260 --> 20:55.140
Are you sure it wasn't just 
a female adventurer or a kobold?

20:55.140 --> 20:58.080
When you put it like that,
I'll admit that I don't know.

20:58.470 --> 21:02.240
My ears were pretty shot 
from all the ruckus, too.

21:02.520 --> 21:04.850
Even if the kobolds have 
a human on their side,

21:04.850 --> 21:08.190
it doesn't change the fact that we
need to make a swift decision.

21:08.440 --> 21:12.660
People are still fighting 
while we stand here.

21:13.090 --> 21:14.150
Hmm...

21:14.150 --> 21:18.980
If all that's true, 
the kobolds aren't the only threat.

21:19.620 --> 21:24.970
There's a possibility that much more savage 
monsters may beset our town...

21:24.970 --> 21:29.340
And if that ever happens, 
we cannot afford to waste manpower.

21:30.130 --> 21:33.060
Very well. Begin the retreat!

21:34.030 --> 21:36.760
Thank goodness.

21:40.990 --> 21:41.840
What in the world?

21:41.840 --> 21:42.650
Lightning!

21:50.710 --> 21:52.360
Where are the kobolds?

21:53.310 --> 21:55.780
Did the lightning take them away?

21:55.780 --> 21:59.530
You can't be serious. 
What's going on with this battle?!

23:35.140 --> 23:39.970
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.140 --> 23:39.970
<b>After the Battle</b>
